  year ernest pulled into the driveway and  parked the two unloaded their bags and  arcadia unlocked the cabin door  once inside they turned everything on  turned up the heat and settled in  this place is sort of like an oasis in  the middle of nothing huh ernest said as  he organized some stuff in the kitchen  yeah it always felt like an escape when  i was a kid like everything was okay  here arcadia responded yeah it's like  somehow both unsettling and comfortable  at the same time i like it though  ernest pulled out a bottle of vodka that  he had gotten from one of his friend's  older brothers and poured two glasses  mixing the liquor with some juice he had  also brought the two sat in the living  room drinking and talking all night  about the same sorts of stuff they  talked about on the drive normalcy of  day-to-day life and school and pop  culture about anecdotes of their pasts  and plans for the future  they laughed and cried and had an  incredible time several hours later  after several drinks arcadia passed out  on the couch ernest was still wide awake  though and so he carefully carried  arcadia into the bedroom made sure she  was okay and then went back into the  living room to watch some tv and  continue to drink by himself  he watched whatever was on late night  basic cable the news then a sports talk  show then a reality show rerun then a  documentary about chimpanzees in one  scene of the documentary it showed how  sometimes male chimpanzees eat other  chimps sometimes even infants in order  to gain territory and breeding  opportunities  something about the sequence of  everything he was watching the unnerving  similarity between some of the scenes in  the news and reality show and some of  the scenes in the nature documentary  suddenly gave ernest a weird feeling in  the pit of his stomach it all made him  think about how he was a living thing in  the world and all the absurdity he was  watching on tv he was also a part of  this then made ernest think about how  all these shows how basically everything  in ordinary life was just a distraction  or neat repackaging of what lied behind  underneath and inside it a meaningless  chaos of absurdity and conflict and  violence and death what's the point of  all this ernest wondered to himself with  an increasing fervency of anxiety he  felt as if a spotlight was suddenly  being shined on some void inside him  compelled by this intense urine for  something he couldn't quite locate  ernest got up  left the cabin and walked out into the  woods  he made his way through a small lining  of dead trees as snow fell down onto his  exposed skin  fairly quickly he reached a large pond  completely frozen over he walked out  onto it he kept walking until the view  of everything around him was completely  clear and wide in all directions  once at the center he looked up at the  clear night sky filled with stars above  him he remembered how he was apparently  made of stuff that came from them this  then made him think about how if he kept  going all the way back tracing back all  the elements of his body and mind in  some strange way he would eventually  reach stars  but this then made him think about what  if he kept going further back what if he  followed what everything he was made of  back before the stars back before the  stuff that made the stars was stuff at  all how far back did it all really go  where did it come from why was it there  why was he here  he thought about how no one really knew  the answers to any of this  this then made him realize that if he  didn't know where the stuff he was made  of came from what did that mean about  where it was going where it would end up  what would happen when he reached the  end of himself when the next stars reach  the end of themselves when the stuff  that made the next stars reach the end  of themselves when everything reached  the end of itself  was this his only experience of  something before nothingness forever was  this the universe's only experience of  somethingness before nothingness forever  what even is nothingness what happens  when we die what happens after  everything dies  if everything ends does anything really  matter how could it suddenly an extreme  frigid pain came over ernest's entire  body it was a feeling unlike he had ever  felt before  then in a sudden shock he realized he  was partly submerged in the freezing  cold water of the pond the surface of  the ground had cracked beneath him and  he was now on the underside of it he  flailed dangerously in a panic pulling  parts of the surface down under with him  as he tried to grab a hold of the edge  after struggling for a few long seconds  he was able to pull himself back up but  now he stood on the surface soaked in  the freezing water uncontrollably  grasping for air and exposed to the cold  world around him  in a delirious panic ernest ran back to  the bank of the pond and then back to  the cabin  when he reached the cabin though it was  gone his car was gone  everything was gone there was only an  empty lot his panic became surreal he  quickly realized he had gone the wrong  way and was now at some sort of campsite  he turned around and ran back the way he  came but his body and mind were now  struggling to function and he had lost  most of his sense of orientation  after going several different directions  all he could seem to find was more dark  cold forest  as time passed ernest became  increasingly lethargic and tired he felt  a visceral intimation of his mortality  as he began to feel his body less and  less  i'm going to die  he thought to himself  i'm going to die  ernest panic soon turned to grief and  dread unsure of what to do and where to  go he sat down beside a fallen tree  huddled himself around himself and  closed his eyes  as he laid there he thought about the  cabin he thought about arcadia he  thought about the warmth and comfort of  that ordinary house heated just to room  temperature a few appliances a tv and  another human being whom he loved  he had never wanted anything so badly in  his entire life  the banal normality of everything on the  surface  as ernest's thoughts began to slow and  spread out more and more separated by  increasingly long intervals of  unconsciousness  suddenly a distorted soft voice of a  woman echoed through the woods and into  ernest's frozen ears  ernest  ernest  disoriented ernest woke back up hello  ernest follow my voice  where are you  just keep following my voice i'm right  here  i'm right here  i'm right here  in a life or death game of existential  marco polo ernest followed arcadia's  voice through the woods for 20 minutes  and then  he saw it  the warm light from the windows of the  cabin  in front the silhouette of arcadia  for that moment he forgot that he was  freezing cold  soaking wet  and going to die  the news can often get a bad rap as it  often should but following the events of  the world is not only useful from a  practical standpoint but sometimes just  staying engaged in this strange game we  are all playing can help our life be  more stimulating and interesting  this video sponsor morningbrew is a free  daily newsletter delivered to your inbox  monday through sunday that makes the  news entertaining easy and succinct  providing the value of staying informed  without all the negative side effects  morning brew works by consolidating the  most relevant news in areas related to  business tech and finance and turns it  into witty light short pieces that get  you up to speed every day in as little  as just five minutes recently morning  brew has made it easy to keep up with  significant changes in the housing stock  and crypto markets as well as the  unusual economic times we're facing  following the various efforts of the  feds to combat inflation like adjusting  interest rates and how these changes  might affect the consumer if you're  interested in keeping up with events and  changes in markets like these or a